kikiri-de is a German-only text-to-speech project. This repository contains
its inference part only. It is written from scratch but reuses and adapts
code from the following open-source projects:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

StyleTTS 2
  Source:  https://github.com/yl4579/StyleTTS2
  License: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Aaron (Yinghao) Li
  Used in: kikiri_de/modules/ (prosody predictor, text encoder, ISTFTNet decoder)

PL-BERT
  Source:  https://github.com/yl4579/PL-BERT
  License: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 Aaron (Yinghao) Li
  Used in: kikiri_de/modules/plbert.py (ALBERT phoneme encoder wrapper)

Kokoro
  Source:  https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro
  License: Apache License 2.0, Copyright hexgrad
  Used in: kikiri_de/modules/ (inference-side module layout), kikiri_de/model.py

kikiri-tts (predecessor project)
  Source:  https://github.com/semidark/kikiri-tts
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Used in: training recipe experience, voicepack extraction approach

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mideki (dependency, not included in this repository)
  Source:  https://github.com/ichDaheim/mideki
  License: Apache License 2.0, derived from misaki (hexgrad, Apache 2.0) via
           github.com/semidark/misaki. Provenance: NOTICE.md in that repository

Model weights and voices (Hugging Face: ichDaheim/kikiri-de, not included here)
  Trained by the kikiri project on the HUI-Audio-Corpus-German and Qwen-TTS
  generated data; contain PL-BERT-de weights (fine-tuned during training).
  The style encoders, which are only needed to create new voices, are not
  included.
